WEBVTT

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.480
She paid you?

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.520
Wait, no. Don't get the wrong idea. 
This is just her thing.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:52.780
<i>Akihiko?</i>

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:55.890
He used to be pretty wild,

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.280
but I think he's calmed 
down quite a bit now.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.910
Yo, we take a right up here.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:03.690
Kaji-san.

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.540
It's not that you've actually calmed down.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:11.550
You just don't do stuff like that 
in front of Haruki-san, right?

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.770
I knew you wanted to go all-out 
to learn more about music,

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:23.530
but I didn't think you'd actually 
come to this concert with me.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.750
Thank you very much for the ticket.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.520
No worries. I didn't pay for them, anyway.

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:38.200
Huh?

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.320
Apparently, he's taken a liking to you.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.250
<i>I'm pretty sure I've seen him before.</i>

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.090
Damn it, I told him to brush his hair...

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.110
Um...

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:41.370
So why is the guy with the violin
 the only one standing?

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.750
That's how violin concertos work.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:03.030
<i>Ugetsu was the first genius 
that I ever encountered.</i>

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.120
<i>His talent was aggressive.</i>

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:17.550
<i>Back then, there was still something 
like aspiration in my music,</i>

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.120
<i>as well as something resembling confidence.</i>

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.350
<i>But that all ended the day I met Ugetsu.</i>

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:32.060
<i>Ever since that day, I've hated him.</i>

00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.060
Kaji-san.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.420
I...

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.340
I... want to write songs.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.850
<Inbox 

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:07.460
Whoa...

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.650
We made it through the second screening...

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:11.590
Second?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.010
Screening for what, now?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.040
Our entry for CAC!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:15.850
Huh?!

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.750
CAC? What's that?

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.650
Countdown-Fes Amateur Contest!

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.510
It's a super huge rock festival
 held at the end of the year.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:27.000
There's a slot where amateurs 
get to play with the pros!

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.830
When did we even apply for that?

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:32.870
Uh, we talked about entering when we 
decided on our band name, remember?!

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.240
Wait, when did we even get 
through the first screening?

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.390
You never mentioned it!

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.060
I <i>definitely</i> told you they 
cleared our application!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.100
So how many screenings are there?

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.380
The third one coming up is the last one.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:46.760
They'll be judging our performance live.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:48.350
A live performance?!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.760
Why are you so happy?!

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.300
Do you understand how big a deal this is?!

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.400
Ue. Down, boy.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:56.580
I wanna do it.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.920
With what? The one song we have?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.310
But it makes me happy.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.070
Seeing all the comments, I mean.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.750
Don't they make you guys happy?

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.000
To be honest...

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.430
I'm ecstatic.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.660
Same.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.910
Good. Because...

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.170
I really want to do this.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:22.550
<b>Karaoke Plaza</b>

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.910
Mafuyu, you said you wanted
 to write songs, right?

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:26.680
Yeah.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.220
Our first song gave me some
 personal closure, basically.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.330
So for our next one, I...

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:42.810
Seriously, <i>what</i>?! Don't just give up 
in the middle of your thought!

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.530
I do have something I want to say.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.980
Just say it, then!

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:46.940
Another time.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:47.950
What?!

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:53.580
<i>After hearing his performance, 
I realized two things.</i>

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:59.400
<i>The first is that you can make 
emotions resonate through music.</i>

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.710
<i>The second</i>

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.120
<i>is that I think Kaji-san is the same as me.</i>

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:09.180
I'm... home.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.860
Are you here, Akihiko?

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:17.430
I'm back in Japan for the first time in ages, 
and you're in bed before me? Seriously?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.690
Hey, so how was the Tchaik concerto?

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.820
Akihiko.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.610
It was probably so good, it made you hard.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:32.870
Aki—

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.920
What? Are we doing this today? That's rare.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:49.590
You never get tired of this, 
do you, Akihiko?

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:55.220
<i>I'm pretty sure Kaji-san is also in love 
with someone he can't replace...</i>

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:58.180
<i>and it's unrequited.</i>

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.820
Akihiko! Someone's here!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.830
Akihiko!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:15.050
Yeah... Just one more minute...

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:17.440
Uh, if you don't answer it now, 
they're gonna leave.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.330
Who is it?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.180
Oh...

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:24.840
Ah! You're the vocalist kid!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:39.120
The hell am I looking at right now?

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.350
Shh.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.020
Yeah, that sucked.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:05.780
So the 6-bar progression after the hook...

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.920
The "lala lala lala" part...

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.630
I think you didn't know what to do, 
so you brought down the intensity.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.640
I bet it's supposed to be 
more like, "Lala lala lala..."

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.020
Those are the emotions 
you wanted to sing, right?

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.000
Mafuyu, is that your new song?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.760
Yes. That's all I've finished so far, though—

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.550
Yeah, yeah, got it.

00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:35.280
I've got plans with Haruki.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.280
Keep Ugetsu company for me.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.110
Huh?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:43.540
A-Are you sure it was okay 
to just leave him there?!

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.520
Sure.

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:47.470
W-Wait, you have a roommate?!

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:48.670
I do.

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:52.650
But, man... Mafuyu's gotten 
so much better, it's scary.

00:08:52.650 --> 00:08:56.710
Everything he's kept bottled up
 inside is finally free,

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.540
so it's probably just all overflowing.

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:00.370
<i>R-Roommate?</i>

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:05.200
He actually had the balls to show up 
at my place unannounced, so yeah.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:09.350
I swear, geniuses just end up 
losing sight of everything else.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:10.860
<i>He has a roommate...</i>

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:13.070
And then there's Uenoyama.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.790
I know he's taking remedial classes, 
but only for two subjects, right?

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.240
I know, right?!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:21.660
Being average at that school means
 you're already super smart!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.250
He's pretty much a borderline genius 
himself. He's got what it takes.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.310
So, Akihiko...

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.270
I know this might not be the best way 
to put it, but you're different.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:38.520
You were in orchestra in college, 
so you're actually a really good violinist,

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.070
and you can play the guitar and bass.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:46.890
But... like, you're super talented overall, 
but you don't excel in any one thing.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:47.940
Wait, was that a diss?

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.350
No!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.400
It's sorta cool being a jack-of-all-trades, 
but a master of none, you know?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.220
Meanwhile, I'm the dictionary 
definition of mediocrity.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.840
But...

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:02.090
I was just thinking that
 must be hard sometimes.

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:07.390
You're the peacemaker.

00:10:07.390 --> 00:10:08.330
Huh?

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:10.710
That's why everyone loves you.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.270
Uh, what?

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:20.600
Nothing. Just saying you're way
 more popular than you think.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.690
Uh, I'm not actually popular with anyone!

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:28.700
Hm... There's nothing here.

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:34.140
Um, Uge... tsu-san, are you and Kaji-san...

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.320
Oh, sleeping together?

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.010
We're not exactly together anymore.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:39.860
Huh?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.200
<i>I met Akihiko in high school.</i>

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.580
<i>And my first love was so much fun.</i>

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:58.390
<i>He spoiled the hell out of me, 
and I became more cowardly.</i>

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.600
<i>But...</i>

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.760
<i>Around the time we graduated high school</i>

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:18.860
<i>and I started working as a violinist, 
I suddenly realized...</i>

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:24.600
<i>that we were suffocating each other 
more than anything else in this world.</i>

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:28.790
Akihiko.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.780
Hm?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.800
Let's end this.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:46.290
With Akihiko around, I don't have
 any freedom with my music,

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:51.200
and my existence overall was 
causing suffering for him, too.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.270
And I think you know the rest.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:58.050
We both spent two years being desperate,

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.030
and somehow, we just keep 
crawling back to each other.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:05.910
Why did you tell me all this?

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:10.160
Well, I don't have any friends.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:14.040
Maybe I just wanted someone to understand.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.040
Even just a little bit.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.670
I'm not very expressive,

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:25.050
so I'm pretty sure Akihiko thinks I'm the worst
 piece of shit ever and hates my guts.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:28.730
I love Akihiko to death,

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.430
and even though I'm the one who dumped 
him, I haven't been able to let go.

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:35.440
I've been trying to get rid of him 
at every opportunity,

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:37.440
but that still hasn't worked out, either.

00:12:38.150 --> 00:12:43.200
All this time... I've been waiting 
for him to finally leave me.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.390
Well, anyway. I'm gonna head out, too.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.590
The place is soundproof, 
so make yourself at home.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:52.070
If you liked that story,

00:12:52.070 --> 00:12:54.780
go ahead and use it as 
inspiration for your new song.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.590
<i>Right around the time we 
first started living together,</i>

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.730
<i>and he tried to give me my first gift...</i>

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.590
<i>For some reason, I hated them so much</i>

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:16.970
<i>that I said I didn't want them
and knocked one out of his hand.</i>

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:23.070
<i>It was just a mug.</i>

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.350
<i>I should've just said I was happy.</i>

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:29.870
<i>I want to stay by his side.</i>

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:31.490
<i>I want to stay by his side.</i>

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:33.750
<i>I want to stay by his side.</i>

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:38.280
<i>Even so... I love music.</i>

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:48.870
<i>But now... I'm sure nothing 
will surpass that.</i>

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:54.860
He's just seriously such a great guy.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.270
<b>Ugetsu Murata</b>

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:00.270
I'm bringing home my new boyfriend.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.650
Mm? What?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.310
What do you mean?

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:12.530
<b>Okonomiyaki</b>

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.230
We talked about doing a get-together 
with the other bands...

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.530
What?! What do you mean, you're not coming?

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.930
I'm in a really shitty mood right now,

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:16.160
<i>so I'm not coming.</i>

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.030
Bu—

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:19.420
<i>Bye.</i>

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.640
<i>That was... a girl.</i>

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:28.120
<i>They were definitely doing it.</i>

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.650
It looked so good!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:31.910
What did?

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:32.550
The udon?

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:33.270
Yeah!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.010
Something happen?

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:34.660
It's super good.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:35.750
It's so simple to make.

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:37.720
I had some sukiyaki broth left over,

00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:40.060
Akihiko seems to be really 
irritable these past few days.

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:40.060
so I just added eggs and tofu 
and mixed them all together.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.200
Oh, and I added some cheese.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:42.910
So that's why you're tired.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.550
I've never made sukiyaki before.

00:14:42.910 --> 00:14:46.110
Seriously, just forget about him already!

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:45.470
Seriously?

00:14:45.470 --> 00:14:47.270
Do you just cook the meat?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.640
Yeah, I mean... yeah...

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:48.640
You chop up some vegetables,

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:51.570
and then stew them with some 
soy sauce, mirin, and sugar.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.460
Hey.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.330
I've never used mirin before.

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.830
Do you even cook?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:57.330
Why not play bass for another band 
for a change of pace?

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:55.670
Not at all.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.000
Char siu boys!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.190
That doesn't count.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.330
As a support bassist.

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.830
Then do you just eat out all the time?

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:01.600
What? In your band?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:03.300
Yeah. I should be saving money,

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:02.640
Nah.

00:15:02.640 --> 00:15:05.080
It's, uh... your ex-girlfriend's band.

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:05.080
but I really don't know how to cook.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.190
Take cooks.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:07.280
My ex-gir... Uh, no!

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:07.890
Yatake-san cooks?

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:10.040
I figured you'd be okay...

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.040
His family sends him veggies all the time.

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:10.970
Okay? Seriously?

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:13.720
He shares some with me 
sometimes, and it's awesome.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.720
More importantly, are <i>you</i> okay?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.780
Lucky.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.450
You don't cook.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.580
You seem really stressed lately.

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:19.110
Maybe if I got some free veggies.

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.830
Are you actually enjoying music lately?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.000
You guys are close.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.220
Yeah. Of course I... am...

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.600
I mean, we get along.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.460
I guess.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.360
You guess?!

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:29.180
<i>But I'm definitely... suffering even more.</i>

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.210
Workin' hard?

00:15:33.210 --> 00:15:34.240
Hey.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.330
Wait, it's just you two?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.480
Where's Akihiko?

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:40.170
He said he couldn't make it 
because of something at school.

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:42.870
<i>School? Really, now?</i>

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:47.350
Well, we just wanted to talk about 
the new song today rather than jam.

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:49.490
Can you take a listen?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:50.310
Sure.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.100
Okay, let's do this.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.010
One, two, three, four.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:08.190
What's for dinner tonight? Udon or pasta...

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.350
Yeah, those aren't the final lyrics yet.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.650
Oh, thank God!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.220
We can probably add in a drum fill here.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:22.000
This is the part we wanted to
 discuss with you, Haruki-san.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.940
<i>Wait, hold up.</i>

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:26.790
<i>Mafuyu's really starting to 
understand how music works.</i>

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.920
<i>When did he learn so much about it?</i>

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:32.030
We don't have any lyrics yet,

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:34.550
and we've only written up 
until the first hook.

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.730
<i>They didn't even have to add 
lyrics for me to realize it.</i>

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:40.930
<i>This is a love song.</i>

00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:42.930
<i>He's a genius.</i>

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:45.180
<i>As the sound spreads, you can feel</i>

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:47.360
<i>the presence of a thousand 
musical pieces behind it.</i>

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.600
<i>He actually put in the work 
and listened to them.</i>

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.800
<i>Just calling him a genius is misleading.</i>

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:53.800
<i>But...</i>

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.320
<i>This feeling I get sometimes 
where I feel like I'm clearly</i>

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:58.610
If we're gonna be judged in October,

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:59.570
<i>a different being than Uenoyama or Mafuyu...</i>

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.280
I'm thinking we can make 
another song by then.

00:16:59.570 --> 00:17:02.320
<i>It comes with a feeling of alienation.</i>

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.190
Even if the sessions are short, I want to
 get into the studio as much as we can.

00:17:02.320 --> 00:17:05.190
<i>Seriously... What even am I?</i>

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:08.290
So let's hold off on doing 
live performances.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:12.260
Huh? Yeah, uh... sure.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:13.920
Thank you.

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.560
Akihiko Kaji
Are you still up?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.570
Akihiko Kaji

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.570
Are you still up?

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.570
I'm awake

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.570
I'm right in front of your place

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.570
Are you still up?

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.570
I'm awake

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.570
I'm right in front of your place

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.570
Can I stay over?

00:17:41.390 --> 00:17:42.200
Hey.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.800
What happened to your face?!

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:51.460
Yeah, so I... sorta got 
into it with my roommate.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.460
"Got into it"?! You had a fist fight?!

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:57.990
So I've been spending the night 
at random places to get by.

00:17:57.990 --> 00:17:58.810
Huh?!

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.470
You mean you haven't been home at all?!

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.260
I mean, it hasn't been <i>that</i> long.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:06.400
<i>He's like the old Akihiko.</i>

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:10.360
How was the studio session today?

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:13.600
Oh... I listened to the new song.

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:17.190
They want to hold off on live performances 
for a while to focus on songwriting.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.000
Guess we'll have to hit the studio 
as much as possible, then.

00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:22.740
You have time during the summer, don't you?

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.130
Um...

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.340
What? You have other plans?

00:18:29.340 --> 00:18:33.390
N-No, I wouldn't actually call them plans...

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:37.310
Are you hiding something?

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:38.140
Huh?

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:41.430
What are you hiding?

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.850
Uh, what's with you?

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.010
Wait, why are you in such a bad mood?

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:46.680
There has to be something.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.640
I mean... Sort of...

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:53.340
I don't wanna hear that from you.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.400
Hey, that hurts!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.020
Just tell me.

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:03.160
My ex-girlfriend asked if I'd fill in 
as a support bassist for a while!

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:05.400
This doesn't even concern you!

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:10.530
So...

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:14.040
Are you going? To your ex-girlfriend?

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:18.740
Things are getting too hard, so you're 
gonna abandon your current band.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:22.050
That's not true... 
I never said anything like—

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.330
You...

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:29.310
You're in love with me, 
but you're gonna run away?

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:35.060
Wh-What are you talking about? 
Wait, why are you...

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:38.550
Why? Who cares anymore?

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.980
Haruki...

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.080
You keep mentioning an ex-girlfriend,

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.690
but are you actually able to sleep 
with any girls when you're like this?

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:53.080
<i>Screw you! You can't be serious!</i>

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.730
<i>I was sleeping with them 
just fine before I met you!</i>

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.400
Wait...

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.090
Akihiko...

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.580
Aki—

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.040
No, wait, wait. Stop! You—

00:20:10.300 --> 00:20:14.480
<i>Damn. I'm just taking out 
my frustration on him.</i>

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:20.110
<b>Ugetsu Murata</b>

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:20.110
I'm bringing home my new boyfriend.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.110
<i>Even after separating, 
Ugetsu and I would clash regularly.</i>

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:26.490
<i>Like he keeps using those opportunities 
to finally let go of me for good.</i>

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:31.000
<i>Like he's trying to tell me 
he doesn't need me</i>

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:35.030
<i>and force me out of his world for good.</i>

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:37.880
<i>Why?</i>

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.700
<i>If you don't want me anymore,</i>

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.380
<i>then why do you still accept
 my attachment to you?</i>

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.740
<i>If you feel so sorry for 
me and my feelings,</i>

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:47.140
<i>why are you trying to throw me away?</i>

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:49.330
<i>I want to hold you.</i>

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.140
<i>I want to run away.</i>

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:52.770
<i>I want to give up on this.</i>

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.140
<i>But I just can't let go of you.</i>

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.270
<i>I want to touch you.</i>

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.650
<i>And it hurts so much.</i>

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.000
Akihiko...

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:13.440
What is it? Please stop...

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.600
Don't make that face...

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:22.080
Please don't look so hurt...

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:25.930
What is it? Tell me, please.

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:28.930
I'll do anything for you.

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:36.060
Telling you won't solve anything.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.070
I'm sorry.

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:46.580
<i>Why couldn't it just be you?</i>

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:53.700
I'm really sorry.

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:58.710
This was completely my fault.

00:22:02.730 --> 00:22:05.890
That's not what I want 
you to apologize for.

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:11.720
I told you I'd do anything. In the end, 
it was basically consensual.

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:14.600
You can spend the night tonight.

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:15.730
What?

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:19.020
I'll go to a friend's place. 
Just leave in the morning.

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:22.980
You can use whatever I have here.

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:25.150
Don't worry about locking 
up when you leave.

00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.310
Haruki—

00:22:27.800 --> 00:22:30.370
I'll hold off on filling in as bass.

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:33.550
So... just be gone in the morning.

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:41.500
<i>Telling you won't solve anything.</i>

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:43.450
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:54.770
Shit!

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:01.270
<i>I rely way too much on Haruki...</i>

00:23:01.920 --> 00:23:05.400
<i>How lame can I be? I have nowhere to go.</i>

00:23:05.420 --> 00:23:08.530
Akihiko

00:23:06.350 --> 00:23:07.520
<i>Basically...</i>

00:23:07.520 --> 00:23:11.570
<i>I haven't had a home ever since my parents 
separated during my last year of high school.</i>

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:14.810
<i>And right when I was trying 
to figure out what to do...</i>

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:16.520
Why don't you come to my place, then?

00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:23.380
<i>From then on, I had a place to call 
home that never got any sunlight.</i>

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:27.610
<i>Whenever I fought with Ugetsu,</i>

00:23:27.610 --> 00:23:30.730
<i>I did whatever it took to find 
another place to stay.</i>

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:35.430
<i>It was pitiful and pathetic... 
and I did things I can't even laugh about.</i>

00:23:36.170 --> 00:23:41.980
<i>But I just... didn't want Haruki 
to find out about any of it.</i>

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:58.060
<i>Oh, God. Something happened.</i>

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:05.210
Akihiko Kaji

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:05.210
Thanks

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:05.210
Hey

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:05.210
Sorry, is Haruki at your place?

00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:05.210
<i>Yeah, something definitely happened!</i>

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:06.960
<b>Yatake</b>

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:09.440
What the hell happened to you?

00:24:09.440 --> 00:24:11.350
Those dark circles are intense!

00:24:11.350 --> 00:24:13.340
This barley tea is delicious.

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:17.910
Seriously, what's going on? It's painfully 
obvious that something happened.

00:24:17.910 --> 00:24:19.240
Please, sir, may I have some more?

00:24:19.240 --> 00:24:21.850
Uh, are you even listening to me?

00:24:23.230 --> 00:24:24.520
Take-chan.

00:24:25.340 --> 00:24:29.360
You always cut your own hair, 
don't you, Take-chan?

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:33.110
Mafuyu Sato

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:33.110
Sorry

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:33.110
But is Haruki at your place?

00:24:31.360 --> 00:24:33.110
He's not

00:24:32.050 --> 00:24:33.110
<i>Shit.</i>

00:24:33.670 --> 00:24:35.770
<i>Haruki hasn't come home yet.</i>

00:24:36.240 --> 00:24:39.630
<i>I ended up waiting because I didn't want
to awkwardly bump into him, but...</i>

00:24:39.630 --> 00:24:41.140
<i>Should I go look for him?</i>

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:42.190
<i>Wait, is he okay?</i>

00:24:42.190 --> 00:24:45.230
<i>Uh, do I need to put in 
a missing person's report?</i>

00:24:51.260 --> 00:24:52.250
Haruki—

00:24:54.470 --> 00:24:57.540
Oh. You're still here.

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:01.320
Huh?

00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:04.140
Hey. Good morning.

00:25:04.140 --> 00:25:06.720
Wh-What happened to your hair?!

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:08.650
It's been too hot, so I cut it.

00:25:09.660 --> 00:25:10.900
You're still here.

00:25:12.200 --> 00:25:16.910
Sorry, but as you can see, I'm pretty 
exhausted since you rejected me.

00:25:16.910 --> 00:25:18.610
Could you just go home?

00:25:18.610 --> 00:25:19.910
H-Hang on a sec—

00:25:22.990 --> 00:25:26.040
Look. I'm actually mad here.

00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:28.770
Sorr—

00:25:28.770 --> 00:25:31.420
I'm saying it pisses me off even more 
when you apologize to me!

00:25:32.520 --> 00:25:35.930
Just go home. For both of our sakes.

00:25:37.460 --> 00:25:39.520
I don't have anywhere I can go.

00:25:39.520 --> 00:25:40.630
Huh?

00:25:40.630 --> 00:25:44.300
I seriously don't have anywhere 
else I can go right now.

00:25:44.300 --> 00:25:47.810
I've been staying a few days 
here and there...

00:25:47.810 --> 00:25:50.260
But I'd be pushing my luck 
if I stayed longer...

00:25:50.890 --> 00:25:52.840
Could I stay here for a while—

00:25:52.840 --> 00:25:54.210
Hell no!

00:25:54.210 --> 00:25:55.110
Right.

00:25:56.910 --> 00:26:01.330
I'll do all the housework... 
And I'll sleep anywhere.

00:26:01.330 --> 00:26:02.590
Even the floor.

00:26:02.590 --> 00:26:03.480
What?!

00:26:03.480 --> 00:26:05.570
I promise I won't try anything again.

00:26:05.570 --> 00:26:09.340
I was at my limit yesterday... 
and I went too far.

00:26:10.140 --> 00:26:11.590
I'm sorry.

00:26:11.590 --> 00:26:13.320
Please help me.

00:26:16.050 --> 00:26:18.990
I would've totally abandoned you 
if we weren't in the same band.

00:26:27.480 --> 00:26:29.100
Hey, wait, stop!

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:31.460
We're totally off today.

00:26:31.940 --> 00:26:35.330
What the hell? Why are you in such
 a bad mood, Haruki-san?

00:26:35.330 --> 00:26:37.400
<i>Yikes!</i>

00:26:37.400 --> 00:26:40.260
Sorry, I'm just a bit off today.

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:42.660
But... I'll be fine.

00:26:47.450 --> 00:26:48.330
Hey!

00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:50.240
Haruki! Hey!

00:26:50.240 --> 00:26:51.580
Stop following me.

00:26:53.740 --> 00:26:55.090
<i>I'm so pathetic.</i>

00:26:56.070 --> 00:26:58.980
<i>Everyone else looks like they're sparkling.</i>

00:27:00.370 --> 00:27:01.590
Haruki!

00:27:01.590 --> 00:27:02.850
<i>I'm so lame.</i>

00:27:03.420 --> 00:27:04.530
<i>It hurts.</i>

00:27:04.530 --> 00:27:05.600
Hey!

00:27:06.240 --> 00:27:08.850
<i>It doesn't matter if it's music
 or anything else...</i>

00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:10.620
<i>Why am I always the one 
who's so desperate?!</i>

00:27:10.620 --> 00:27:11.850
Damn it, wait!

00:27:13.420 --> 00:27:15.730
Am I even necessary?!

00:27:16.200 --> 00:27:19.410
I'm not a genius like everyone else.

00:27:19.410 --> 00:27:21.980
And I was way off playing 
with you guys today!

00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:26.420
<i>I'm so pathetic. I want to disappear.</i>

00:27:26.420 --> 00:27:27.670
What?

00:27:27.670 --> 00:27:30.860
That's because you were looking down 
the whole time you were playing.

00:27:32.070 --> 00:27:34.630
Of course you'd be off if you don't look up.

00:27:35.420 --> 00:27:39.290
You don't have to look in front of you, 
but at least look at me.

00:27:39.290 --> 00:27:41.870
Being in a band is different 
than being a solo artist.

00:27:42.710 --> 00:27:46.240
A band would never work 
out with four geniuses.

00:27:47.420 --> 00:27:52.480
Someone has to be there to
 support them, and we need you.

00:27:52.980 --> 00:27:55.230
I'm pretty sure I tell you that all the time.

00:27:59.360 --> 00:28:00.950
Any objections?

00:28:00.950 --> 00:28:02.440
No...

00:28:02.830 --> 00:28:04.740
Who the hell do you think you're talking to?

00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:07.780
What do you want for dinner?

00:28:07.780 --> 00:28:09.880
I'll make you something
 if you're feeling down.

00:28:10.550 --> 00:28:12.750
I am a freeloader, after all.

00:28:12.750 --> 00:28:15.170
You've got this mooching lifestyle down.

00:28:15.170 --> 00:28:16.360
Damn straight.

00:28:17.630 --> 00:28:21.420
<i>And that was the start of 
our bizarre life together.</i>

00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:33.710
<i>Akihiko was far louder 
than I could've ever imagined.</i>

00:28:40.780 --> 00:28:42.530
Please accept this meal

00:28:43.060 --> 00:28:46.450
Our bass and drums are
 really in sync lately.

00:28:46.450 --> 00:28:47.980
Oh, really?

00:28:47.980 --> 00:28:49.470
Did something happen?

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:51.160
No, not really.

00:28:59.110 --> 00:29:02.980
<i>It was just obvious to me that
 Akihiko could do anything.</i>

00:29:04.110 --> 00:29:09.020
<i>I guess I wasn't actually paying 
attention to Akihiko at all.</i>

00:29:11.880 --> 00:29:17.050
<i>It's really not fair that
 I can't actually hate him.</i>

00:29:26.110 --> 00:29:27.700
Oh, right.

00:29:27.700 --> 00:29:29.900
Today's the fireworks festival.

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:31.880
This place is pretty high up,

00:29:31.880 --> 00:29:34.060
so you get a good view, even from far away.

00:29:34.060 --> 00:29:36.050
Must be nice.

00:29:36.050 --> 00:29:38.230
You couldn't see them from your place?

00:29:38.810 --> 00:29:39.960
Not at all.

00:29:40.670 --> 00:29:42.570
I mean, the place was half underground.

00:29:42.570 --> 00:29:46.050
I didn't even know they did 
fireworks around this time for Bon.

00:29:46.470 --> 00:29:49.350
It's sorta freaking me out, actually.

00:29:51.070 --> 00:29:54.730
Didn't you ever go see fireworks with... them?

00:29:55.420 --> 00:29:56.980
Nope.

00:29:58.350 --> 00:30:01.980
But these are prettier 
than I thought they'd be.

00:30:09.080 --> 00:30:12.660
We're pretty much done.

00:30:12.660 --> 00:30:15.700
More like I was basically a friend 
with benefits and a freeloader.

00:30:15.700 --> 00:30:18.000
We weren't technically dating.

00:30:18.510 --> 00:30:20.660
He dumped me a long time ago,

00:30:20.660 --> 00:30:24.540
and I'm just left dangling.

00:30:26.180 --> 00:30:30.010
What the hell? You're totally
 in love with him, though.

00:30:31.430 --> 00:30:33.020
I sure was.

00:30:33.950 --> 00:30:37.100
But now... it just hurts.

00:30:45.400 --> 00:30:50.420
Hey... Thanks for letting me stay here.

00:30:51.280 --> 00:30:53.000
You're welcome.

00:30:57.060 --> 00:30:59.290
Great job today!

00:30:59.780 --> 00:31:02.190
We don't have lyrics yet, but...

00:31:02.190 --> 00:31:03.100
Yeah.

00:31:03.820 --> 00:31:05.810
I'll send the recording to you guys later.

00:31:05.810 --> 00:31:07.660
Make sure you all check your parts.

00:31:07.660 --> 00:31:08.670
Okay.

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:12.240
Haruki, you got plans after this?

00:31:12.240 --> 00:31:13.570
Nope.

00:31:13.570 --> 00:31:16.680
I'm gonna hit the drums a bit more. 
Wanna help me practice?

00:31:16.680 --> 00:31:18.530
Where'd this come from?

00:31:18.530 --> 00:31:21.520
I'm just having a lot of fun.

00:31:24.400 --> 00:31:27.440
I think we need a different approach.

00:31:27.440 --> 00:31:28.370
Huh?

00:31:28.370 --> 00:31:30.110
To the lyrics.

00:31:30.110 --> 00:31:33.690
You said you wanted to write 
a different kind of song.

00:31:35.460 --> 00:31:39.080
It's not like I don't have any ideas at all.

00:31:39.630 --> 00:31:42.680
But when I feel like I've almost got it,

00:31:42.680 --> 00:31:45.330
I keep feeling there's a piece missing.

00:31:46.750 --> 00:31:48.610
Then why don't you go look for it?

00:31:49.430 --> 00:31:52.870
You're the type that gets inspiration 
from your own feelings

00:31:52.870 --> 00:31:56.430
or what's going on with 
the people around you.

00:31:58.160 --> 00:32:00.100
Yikes...

00:32:00.100 --> 00:32:03.910
Yeah, the last train took off ages ago.

00:32:03.910 --> 00:32:06.130
It's such a waste to call a cab.

00:32:06.130 --> 00:32:07.700
And that's why we walk.

00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:08.410
Huh?

00:32:08.410 --> 00:32:10.220
We just walk.

00:32:10.860 --> 00:32:13.910
Wait, what? You mean 
all the way to my place?

00:32:13.910 --> 00:32:14.790
Are you insane?

00:32:14.790 --> 00:32:17.350
It'd probably take us about an hour.

00:32:17.350 --> 00:32:18.430
Are you nuts?

00:32:18.430 --> 00:32:21.220
No, really. An hour goes by fast.

00:32:21.220 --> 00:32:22.850
Seriously...

00:32:22.850 --> 00:32:25.900
You think like a 20-year-old college student.

00:32:28.880 --> 00:32:30.880
Come on, stop that.

00:32:30.880 --> 00:32:33.440
How'd you even find that?

00:32:33.440 --> 00:32:35.140
It was hanging off some grass.

00:32:35.140 --> 00:32:36.840
It's a dragonfly.

00:32:36.840 --> 00:32:39.070
Put the poor thing back.

00:32:39.070 --> 00:32:40.310
Aww.

00:32:40.990 --> 00:32:42.670
What are you, five?

00:32:42.670 --> 00:32:44.470
Bugs are awesome, though.

00:32:44.470 --> 00:32:47.380
Well, I guess I used to catch them 
all the time when I was a kid.

00:32:47.380 --> 00:32:48.830
Oniyanma dragonflies and stuff.

00:32:50.900 --> 00:32:52.590
Was that the first train?

00:32:52.590 --> 00:32:53.640
I believe so.

00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:56.600
You idiot! This is all because 
you kept taking detours!

00:33:08.180 --> 00:33:10.140
I'm so sweaty.

00:33:10.140 --> 00:33:12.140
I don't want to take another step.

00:33:12.810 --> 00:33:15.390
I guess I'll at least take a shower.

00:33:15.390 --> 00:33:17.430
Wow, good boy.

00:33:17.990 --> 00:33:20.120
I can't anymore.

00:33:33.140 --> 00:33:34.500
I'm home.

00:33:35.990 --> 00:33:37.450
Welcome back.

00:33:38.590 --> 00:33:39.640
What?

00:33:39.640 --> 00:33:43.680
I was just thinking you play 
your violin more than I realized.

00:33:44.230 --> 00:33:47.630
Nah, I don't practice near as much
as someone who's hardcore.

00:33:47.630 --> 00:33:48.710
Really?

00:33:49.250 --> 00:33:52.710
Come to think of it, isn't there some
 famous musician from our school?

00:33:53.150 --> 00:33:56.470
He plays the violin... 
What was his name again?

00:33:56.470 --> 00:33:58.900
Oh, Ugetsu Murata.

00:34:06.050 --> 00:34:07.850
Um, I...

00:34:11.510 --> 00:34:12.860
Ah...

00:34:13.510 --> 00:34:15.070
Jeez, you scared me.

00:34:15.070 --> 00:34:16.500
Oh, sorry.

00:34:16.500 --> 00:34:19.620
Your door was unlocked, 
and I heard a loud noise.

00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:23.620
I thought Akihiko came home.

00:34:23.620 --> 00:34:25.870
Wait, Kaji-san's not here?

00:34:27.370 --> 00:34:29.480
Did you come here to see Akihiko?

00:34:29.480 --> 00:34:32.000
I-I came to see you, Ugetsu-san!

00:34:33.470 --> 00:34:34.660
Me?!

00:34:35.010 --> 00:34:37.890
<i>Exceptionally hot days will 
continue into September.</i>

00:34:37.890 --> 00:34:41.650
<i>Due to an autumn rain front, 
we will probably see some rain</i>

00:34:41.650 --> 00:34:45.270
<i>in the Tohoku and Hokuriku 
regions in the morning.</i>

00:34:43.510 --> 00:34:44.580
Morning.

00:34:45.690 --> 00:34:49.550
<i>Parts of western and eastern 
Japan will probably see some sun.</i>

00:34:47.070 --> 00:34:48.530
Morning...

00:34:49.550 --> 00:34:53.480
<i>It seems like Akihiko just spaces out lately.</i>

00:34:50.400 --> 00:34:53.910
<i>The temperatures will
 undoubtedly rise during the day,</i>

00:34:53.910 --> 00:34:57.050
<i>so please take the proper 
precautions against heatstroke.</i>

00:34:57.030 --> 00:34:59.530
<b>[Countdown-fes.A.C] Third screening 
(Final screening) date and time</b>

00:35:01.710 --> 00:35:02.780
Mafuyu!

00:35:03.220 --> 00:35:06.040
Apparently, the day they'll 
be judging us has been set.

00:35:06.910 --> 00:35:08.170
You think you can make it?

00:35:08.170 --> 00:35:09.090
Yeah.

00:35:09.980 --> 00:35:12.040
The lyrics are done.

00:35:12.680 --> 00:35:13.800
We can do this.

00:35:28.180 --> 00:35:29.060
Akihiko Kaji

00:35:33.190 --> 00:35:35.190
Haruki Nakayama

00:35:40.570 --> 00:35:42.950
Voting Slip

00:35:40.950 --> 00:35:42.950
Here's your voting slip.

00:35:46.160 --> 00:35:48.350
I thought the judging 
for these performances

00:35:48.350 --> 00:35:52.480
was going to be more like an audition.

00:35:53.720 --> 00:35:56.050
Make sure you pay attention to everything.

00:35:56.050 --> 00:35:58.150
We're up tomorrow.

00:35:58.150 --> 00:35:59.090
Yup.

00:35:59.090 --> 00:36:00.970
I'm here!

00:36:01.280 --> 00:36:02.390
Haruki-san.

00:36:02.390 --> 00:36:05.470
Sorry, things got a bit chaotic when I left.

00:36:06.110 --> 00:36:07.510
Is it about to start?

00:36:07.510 --> 00:36:10.600
Yeah. Actually, where's Kaji-san?

00:36:10.600 --> 00:36:12.660
Is he not going to make it?

00:36:12.660 --> 00:36:15.160
Um... Yeah.

00:36:34.640 --> 00:36:35.840
Akihiko.

00:36:40.550 --> 00:36:41.480
Here.

00:36:42.130 --> 00:36:43.470
Drink up.

00:36:45.550 --> 00:36:46.280
Sure.

00:36:50.060 --> 00:36:51.140
So, hey.

00:36:52.110 --> 00:36:54.770
I'm leaving this place.

00:36:57.380 --> 00:37:01.250
I came by to at least grab 
my long-sleeved clothes today.

00:37:02.620 --> 00:37:04.460
Oh. I see.

00:37:05.030 --> 00:37:06.940
Yeah.

00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:11.580
Your room is way too messy.

00:37:11.580 --> 00:37:13.170
Shut up.

00:37:13.170 --> 00:37:16.180
Want me to make you 
some food before I leave?

00:37:16.180 --> 00:37:18.490
Who are you, my mom?

00:37:20.980 --> 00:37:25.080
Why? Why are you leaving now?

00:37:27.060 --> 00:37:30.460
Music's actually been fun lately.

00:37:31.420 --> 00:37:35.930
I continued playing the violin 
so I could be your equal.

00:37:36.560 --> 00:37:39.560
I was convinced that this was all I had,

00:37:40.070 --> 00:37:41.970
and that you were all I had.

00:37:43.050 --> 00:37:45.960
But I was suffering that whole time.

00:37:46.830 --> 00:37:51.190
When you said you wanted to break up with me, 
I wanted to run to something else.

00:37:51.830 --> 00:37:54.990
When I started the drums to spite you,

00:37:54.990 --> 00:37:58.120
I thought it was easier 
than doing classical music.

00:37:58.120 --> 00:38:00.370
My overall passion for music 
was pretty much gone.

00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:01.960
But...

00:38:04.560 --> 00:38:06.470
I want to leave this place.

00:38:07.060 --> 00:38:10.480
I want to leave here and play different music.

00:38:14.530 --> 00:38:15.600
No.

00:38:19.980 --> 00:38:21.320
No!

00:38:23.720 --> 00:38:25.040
Why?

00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:29.740
<b>Akihiko Kaji</b>

00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:29.740
<b></b>Call me when you get home

00:38:28.890 --> 00:38:29.740
Haruki-san.

00:38:30.360 --> 00:38:31.580
Haruki-san!

00:38:32.240 --> 00:38:36.290
I said, do you want me 
to take your cup back?

00:38:36.710 --> 00:38:39.500
Oh... Sorry.

00:38:39.860 --> 00:38:41.380
Thanks.

00:38:42.110 --> 00:38:44.760
Are you worried about Kaji-san?

00:38:44.760 --> 00:38:46.510
Y-Yeah...

00:38:46.970 --> 00:38:48.840
You're living together now, right?

00:38:48.840 --> 00:38:49.890
What?!

00:38:49.890 --> 00:38:52.550
H-How much do you...

00:38:52.550 --> 00:38:54.350
Not much, actually.

00:38:54.350 --> 00:38:55.320
Huh?

00:38:55.950 --> 00:38:59.270
But it's hard watching you two sometimes.

00:38:59.270 --> 00:39:00.340
Huh?

00:39:00.800 --> 00:39:02.260
Because, I mean...

00:39:02.720 --> 00:39:05.110
You're in love with Kaji-san, right?

00:39:08.260 --> 00:39:11.310
Have I always been that obvious?

00:39:11.960 --> 00:39:13.680
Well, sort of.

00:39:13.680 --> 00:39:15.910
I-I see...

00:39:16.610 --> 00:39:18.790
But it's okay.

00:39:18.790 --> 00:39:21.190
He's just staying over for a while.

00:39:21.190 --> 00:39:23.290
There's nothing going on between us.

00:39:23.290 --> 00:39:27.340
I crashed and burned, so I don't 
feel that way anymore.

00:39:27.910 --> 00:39:29.300
Really?

00:39:30.550 --> 00:39:31.580
What?

00:39:36.060 --> 00:39:41.060
<i>I mean, it's not like my feelings for
 him just suddenly disappeared.</i>

00:39:43.900 --> 00:39:47.070
<i>But knowing that the one you like 
doesn't want anything from you</i>

00:39:47.070 --> 00:39:48.640
<i>hurts.</i>

00:39:53.670 --> 00:39:55.200
Welcome back.

00:40:00.800 --> 00:40:02.290
What are you doing?

00:40:02.290 --> 00:40:03.130
Mm.

00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:05.500
Did you forget your key?

00:40:05.500 --> 00:40:07.040
No, I have it.

00:40:08.160 --> 00:40:09.790
What happened to your face?

00:40:09.790 --> 00:40:10.740
Mm.

00:40:11.990 --> 00:40:13.360
Haruki.

00:40:13.360 --> 00:40:14.720
What?

00:40:15.690 --> 00:40:16.910
I'm home.

00:40:21.190 --> 00:40:22.600
Just so you know,

00:40:23.440 --> 00:40:28.460
I'm still mad at you, but let me 
calm down over a smoke first.

00:40:31.610 --> 00:40:32.660
Huh?

00:40:34.910 --> 00:40:36.740
I'm gonna run to the convenience stor—

00:40:37.800 --> 00:40:38.870
Huh?!

00:40:39.200 --> 00:40:40.940
Don't go right now.

00:40:45.340 --> 00:40:46.930
Stay right here with me.

00:40:50.880 --> 00:40:52.870
That was amazing.

00:40:52.870 --> 00:40:55.200
Yeah, it was.

00:40:55.200 --> 00:40:57.010
They were all really good.

00:40:59.410 --> 00:41:00.310
What?

00:41:00.870 --> 00:41:03.020
Wh-What?! Wh-What is it?!

00:41:05.470 --> 00:41:07.760
What should I do? 
I'm starting to get nervous.

00:41:07.760 --> 00:41:10.150
What?! You actually get nervous?

00:41:10.930 --> 00:41:15.700
I start to wonder if I'll be able to sing 
this right or not... and I get scared.

00:41:16.820 --> 00:41:19.910
I want to get these feelings across. 
I want them to understand.

00:41:21.590 --> 00:41:23.290
I think I'm getting a little greedy.

00:41:25.200 --> 00:41:27.290
You've changed...

00:41:29.030 --> 00:41:33.110
At first, you were like, "I can't join a band. 
I'm not thinking about anything.

00:41:33.110 --> 00:41:36.430
I can't express myself." You were all hesitant.

00:41:40.410 --> 00:41:41.480
Come here.

00:41:44.430 --> 00:41:48.260
Don't worry. You're way cooler than anyone else.

00:41:48.260 --> 00:41:49.230
Yes, sir.

00:41:49.230 --> 00:41:51.090
Why the "sir"?

00:41:58.820 --> 00:42:02.340
Thanks. Could we get some bass next?

00:42:05.040 --> 00:42:06.580
<i>Why...</i>

00:42:06.860 --> 00:42:09.380
You're going to abandon 
the violin just like that?!

00:42:12.830 --> 00:42:13.980
Whatever.

00:42:14.910 --> 00:42:16.040
Get out.

00:42:19.300 --> 00:42:24.400
<i>Maybe if I just gave up on music, 
everything in my life would work out.</i>

00:42:27.850 --> 00:42:29.100
Come on, now.

00:42:29.100 --> 00:42:31.300
Look at that pathetic face.

00:42:32.870 --> 00:42:35.890
<i>Number 14, given, you're up.</i>

00:42:38.400 --> 00:42:43.530
<i>Before, it took everything 
 I had to let my own words out.</i>

00:42:45.560 --> 00:42:47.110
Come on, get started.

00:42:47.110 --> 00:42:49.560
He's really building up to it.

00:42:51.310 --> 00:42:53.210
<i>My feelings for Uenoyama-kun.</i>

00:42:53.880 --> 00:42:56.780
<i>My love. Someone else's love.</i>

00:42:57.470 --> 00:42:59.130
<i>New music.</i>

00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:02.760
<i>Having others resonate with you.</i>

00:43:04.890 --> 00:43:10.170
Even if I can't sleep, a new day will dawn

00:43:10.170 --> 00:43:17.280
And I sit here staring at it

00:43:24.360 --> 00:43:35.110
Even though this white wall is unchanging

00:43:32.500 --> 00:43:34.500
<i>What was that just now?</i>

00:43:35.110 --> 00:43:45.900
The morning sun shines on it, 
and the clock moves forward

00:43:44.820 --> 00:43:46.600
<i>This feeling...</i>

00:43:45.900 --> 00:43:56.390
I keep moving further away

00:43:47.690 --> 00:43:48.830
<i>It's almost like...</i>

00:43:56.390 --> 00:44:08.240
From the seasons we spent together

00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:16.000
Yet I just want to drift through

00:44:18.240 --> 00:44:19.560
This night

00:44:18.830 --> 00:44:19.880
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:44:19.560 --> 00:44:24.910
Even if I can't sleep, a new day will dawn

00:44:21.200 --> 00:44:22.840
<i>Damn.</i>

00:44:23.880 --> 00:44:28.350
<i>How long has it been since 
I got goosebumps like this?</i>

00:44:24.910 --> 00:44:30.150
And I sit here staring at it

00:44:29.950 --> 00:44:31.180
<i>When...</i>

00:44:30.150 --> 00:44:35.520
The things that are changing, 
the things that are ending

00:44:32.700 --> 00:44:36.090
<i>When did I start hating music?</i>

00:44:35.520 --> 00:44:40.670
The things that are about to begin

00:44:40.670 --> 00:44:46.190
Even though you're gone, I can go on living

00:44:43.530 --> 00:44:45.820
<i>I loved it so much.</i>

00:44:46.190 --> 00:44:51.750
In the end, that makes me sad

00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:50.350
<i>But when I heard Ugetsu 
play for the first time,</i>

00:44:50.350 --> 00:44:53.600
<i>I had the same goosebumps I have right now.</i>

00:44:51.750 --> 00:44:57.000
See? Soon now, a new day will dawn

00:44:56.180 --> 00:45:00.250
<i>Yeah... I love music.</i>

00:44:57.000 --> 00:45:01.300
A new day will dawn

00:45:03.040 --> 00:45:13.610
It blooms in the spring 
and withers in the fall

00:45:06.550 --> 00:45:07.990
<i>Ah...</i>

00:45:09.270 --> 00:45:11.620
<i>When I saw their performance last time,</i>

00:45:12.180 --> 00:45:15.590
<i>I had a feeling that if he had
 some kind of trigger,</i>

00:45:13.660 --> 00:45:25.620
But still, it sprouts again, over and over

00:45:15.590 --> 00:45:17.540
<i>he could really turn into something.</i>

00:45:19.570 --> 00:45:22.570
<i>I guess this is where I got 
to see the answer.</i>

00:45:26.740 --> 00:45:28.660
<i>Oh, I see...</i>

00:45:29.750 --> 00:45:33.500
I realize that it's not what has passed

00:45:30.410 --> 00:45:32.460
<i>So he's the one.</i>

00:45:35.530 --> 00:45:36.990
But what's about to happen

00:45:36.990 --> 00:45:42.420
Even if I can't sleep, a new day will dawn

00:45:42.420 --> 00:45:47.580
I'll eventually have to let go of your hand

00:45:47.580 --> 00:45:52.760
Even if I'm left at a loss 
and cry my eyes out

00:45:52.760 --> 00:45:57.570
I'll eventually stop crying

00:45:58.010 --> 00:46:03.470
Even though you're gone, I can go on living

00:46:03.470 --> 00:46:08.700
Even if I can't be loved, 
I still want to see you

00:46:08.700 --> 00:46:14.080
See? Soon now, a new day will dawn

00:46:14.080 --> 00:46:19.140
A new day will dawn

00:46:24.050 --> 00:46:30.260
Over and over, I've thought about what 
I'd do if Akihiko never came back.

00:46:31.110 --> 00:46:39.230
When there's a wish that we 
don't know will ever come true

00:46:31.780 --> 00:46:35.270
No matter how many times I thought 
about it, I couldn't imagine it clearly.

00:46:38.070 --> 00:46:43.020
I'd think he'd suddenly come 
home tomorrow... or maybe not.

00:46:39.230 --> 00:46:45.100
We call it hope

00:46:45.100 --> 00:46:46.900
But at the same time,

00:46:46.080 --> 00:46:51.660
Even though you're gone, 
a new day will dawn

00:46:47.920 --> 00:46:51.660
I want this pain to end just as much.

00:46:51.660 --> 00:46:57.000
My hand is empty now, but one day 
I'll find another hand to hold

00:46:55.950 --> 00:46:58.510
But at the same time,

00:46:57.000 --> 00:47:07.030
After the long night, we discover the light

00:46:58.510 --> 00:47:03.110
I don't want all the things 
filling this room to disappear.

00:47:07.350 --> 00:47:12.940
That's why even if we're 
scared, we can live on

00:47:08.330 --> 00:47:10.830
Maybe something will remain.

00:47:12.180 --> 00:47:14.520
Even if we can never be the same again...

00:47:12.940 --> 00:47:18.200
So long as the sun rises, 
we can take that step forward again

00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.180
Even if we go somewhere far away...

00:47:18.200 --> 00:47:23.310
See? Soon now, a new day will dawn

00:47:18.750 --> 00:47:22.600
I hope at least the music will remain.

00:47:23.310 --> 00:47:26.440
So don't worry

00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:28.820
<i>It'll be okay.</i>

00:47:28.820 --> 00:47:34.080
See? Not long now, 
it's just around the corner

00:47:30.700 --> 00:47:34.060
<i>You'll be able to go wherever you want.</i>

00:47:34.060 --> 00:47:39.080
A new day will dawn

00:47:37.270 --> 00:47:38.540
<i>Let this reach you!</i>

00:47:47.920 --> 00:47:49.580
Thank you so much.

00:47:57.400 --> 00:48:00.140
Can we have the next act get ready?

00:48:01.140 --> 00:48:02.200
Haruki!

00:48:03.170 --> 00:48:05.820
I need to go see someone off to the station!

00:48:06.390 --> 00:48:08.820
Sure, but the next act is gonna start soon.

00:48:09.870 --> 00:48:11.570
I'll be right back!

00:48:15.470 --> 00:48:16.930
I'll see you in a bit.

00:48:28.330 --> 00:48:29.730
Ugetsu!

00:48:29.730 --> 00:48:31.280
Hey, Ugetsu!

00:48:31.280 --> 00:48:32.730
Hey, stop!

00:48:32.730 --> 00:48:33.840
No.

00:48:33.840 --> 00:48:35.180
Huh?! Wha—

00:48:35.180 --> 00:48:38.600
Because... if I stop, you're going to 
talk about breaking up, aren't you?

00:48:39.760 --> 00:48:41.480
You did great on the drums.

00:48:42.200 --> 00:48:44.950
Seemed delicate as usual, though.

00:48:45.980 --> 00:48:47.140
Hey!

00:48:49.730 --> 00:48:51.130
Hey, listen to me!

00:48:54.160 --> 00:48:56.990
I... love the violin!

00:48:57.990 --> 00:48:59.990
Playing the drums is fun,

00:49:00.460 --> 00:49:03.450
but everything I poured 
into playing violin isn't a lie!

00:49:04.960 --> 00:49:06.850
What the hell?

00:49:06.850 --> 00:49:08.590
So you <i>are</i> breaking up with me.

00:49:10.190 --> 00:49:11.460
Yeah.

00:49:12.200 --> 00:49:13.460
Sorry.

00:49:14.970 --> 00:49:17.720
And I'm sorry for how much
 I've hurt you over the years.

00:49:18.180 --> 00:49:19.470
Thank you.

00:49:21.240 --> 00:49:22.650
I'll be rooting for you.

00:49:26.310 --> 00:49:28.650
I get it, so could you just let go?

00:49:51.420 --> 00:49:52.670
<i>It'll be okay.</i>

00:49:58.370 --> 00:50:01.120
Bye-bye, Akihiko.

00:50:05.540 --> 00:50:06.930
You sure you'll be okay?

00:50:06.930 --> 00:50:08.540
You've got a place to stay?

00:50:08.950 --> 00:50:10.020
Yeah.

00:50:10.630 --> 00:50:12.350
Thank you for everything.

00:50:13.990 --> 00:50:19.030
<i>After all that, we failed in 
the very last stage of judging.</i>

00:50:19.520 --> 00:50:21.450
<i>It's not like we actually 
thought we'd make it,</i>

00:50:21.450 --> 00:50:23.540
<i>but we didn't think we'd fail, either.</i>

00:50:23.540 --> 00:50:25.540
<i>It was super frustrating...</i>

00:50:26.040 --> 00:50:28.790
<i>But we had a lot of people approach us.</i>

00:50:29.710 --> 00:50:33.900
<i>Akihiko started showing up at the studio 
all prepared before anyone else.</i>

00:50:34.500 --> 00:50:36.630
<i>He quit all his part-time jobs,</i>

00:50:36.630 --> 00:50:39.760
<i>and I started seeing him 
at school more often.</i>

00:50:41.540 --> 00:50:43.970
<i>Then we rang in the new year.</i>

00:50:44.790 --> 00:50:48.390
<i>I kept playing with given while filling 
in as bassist for another band</i>

00:50:48.390 --> 00:50:50.420
<i>and played quite a few shows.</i>

00:50:51.780 --> 00:50:53.020
Haruki!

00:50:53.360 --> 00:50:55.030
Here! This is for you!

00:50:55.030 --> 00:50:56.360
Uh... Thanks...

00:50:57.570 --> 00:50:59.960
You've been acting weird lately.

00:50:59.960 --> 00:51:02.370
Yeah, sure. You're welcome.

00:51:03.620 --> 00:51:05.500
<i>And then spring arrived.</i>

00:51:06.350 --> 00:51:09.870
<i>Akihiko entered a violin competition.</i>

00:51:10.820 --> 00:51:12.730
<i>Somewhere deep down,</i>

00:51:12.730 --> 00:51:16.630
<i>I didn't think Akihiko had that
 kind of intense passion in him.</i>

00:51:17.690 --> 00:51:22.390
<i>Wait... Was Akihiko Kaji always like this?</i>

00:51:23.950 --> 00:51:27.230
Sorry. I'm not feeling well, 
so I'm gonna head home.

00:51:27.230 --> 00:51:28.180
Huh?

00:51:33.190 --> 00:51:35.150
<i>Akihiko changed.</i>

00:51:35.590 --> 00:51:39.400
<i>And I ended up imagining who could've
 been the one to change him.</i>

00:51:41.910 --> 00:51:43.160
Akihiko?

00:51:43.160 --> 00:51:44.660
Seriously!

00:51:44.660 --> 00:51:46.720
You should've told me you'd be there!

00:51:46.720 --> 00:51:48.670
I noticed you while I was on 
and almost said something!

00:51:48.670 --> 00:51:50.160
Seriously, why were you there?!

00:51:51.250 --> 00:51:54.120
Mafuyu just invited me out 
of nowhere this morning...

00:51:54.120 --> 00:51:58.060
I was so embarrassed! 
So God damn embarrassed!

00:51:58.060 --> 00:52:00.470
Huh? But you looked really cool and all...

00:52:00.470 --> 00:52:03.320
Well, thanks! How are you feeling?!

00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:04.180
Uh, yeah...

00:52:05.030 --> 00:52:07.430
How'd the results go?

00:52:11.710 --> 00:52:12.650
I placed fourth.

00:52:12.650 --> 00:52:14.710
Huh? Congrats?

00:52:14.710 --> 00:52:17.040
It's not actually that great.

00:52:17.040 --> 00:52:20.200
But... thanks.

00:52:22.810 --> 00:52:27.200
I ended up breaking up with Ugetsu, 
the guy I was in love with.

00:52:27.200 --> 00:52:28.110
Huh?

00:52:28.580 --> 00:52:31.710
You just up and left my place, so I thought...

00:52:31.710 --> 00:52:34.300
Actually, I ended up 
apologizing to my parents

00:52:34.300 --> 00:52:36.460
and asked if they could 
help me out with some cash.

00:52:36.460 --> 00:52:39.450
Then you started getting really 
serious about the violin!

00:52:39.450 --> 00:52:43.350
That's because... I'd been 
running away all this time,

00:52:43.350 --> 00:52:45.470
so I wanted to see just how much I could do.

00:52:45.470 --> 00:52:48.400
And you suddenly started 
acting all distant with me!

00:52:48.400 --> 00:52:49.390
That's because...

00:52:49.390 --> 00:52:51.460
And you just kept on changing!

00:52:51.460 --> 00:52:53.350
Ugh, would you shut up for a second?!

00:52:53.350 --> 00:52:56.610
The reason I decided to make 
changes in my life was because...

00:52:56.610 --> 00:52:59.680
I wanted to become a man 
worthy of your love!

00:53:17.640 --> 00:53:18.840
Haruki.

00:53:20.270 --> 00:53:21.630
Haruki...

00:53:22.260 --> 00:53:24.630
May I touch you?

00:53:31.500 --> 00:53:32.510
Sure.

00:53:35.790 --> 00:53:37.020
I love you.

00:53:37.590 --> 00:53:39.640
Please go out with me.

00:53:41.020 --> 00:53:44.740
We can't go back anymore

00:53:48.880 --> 00:53:58.220
This new pain we felt 
while waiting for the spring

00:53:58.220 --> 00:54:05.550
We jumbled our love 
and dreams into it and ran

00:54:05.910 --> 00:54:11.170
These scars we gained while
 playfully messing around

00:54:11.170 --> 00:54:16.440
That seem to fade but just won't disappear

00:54:16.440 --> 00:54:21.120
We'll be walking away from a place

00:54:21.120 --> 00:54:23.690
That's different from 
where we piled them on

00:54:23.690 --> 00:54:26.980
Putting the days we spent sobbing behind us

00:54:26.980 --> 00:54:32.180
I'm going to go

00:54:32.180 --> 00:54:37.000
See? Just watch me

00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:39.970
We laughed during the fun times

00:54:39.970 --> 00:54:42.620
We got mad over misunderstandings

00:54:42.620 --> 00:54:48.010
I'm going to make our dream come true

00:54:48.010 --> 00:54:57.870
Whenever I'm sad, 
whenever I'm in a lot of pain

00:54:57.870 --> 00:55:03.690
I'll use the memories I recall 
and the time we spent together

00:55:03.690 --> 00:55:10.650
As a backrest for my heart to lean on

00:55:11.490 --> 00:55:20.820
The next time we look behind us

00:55:20.820 --> 00:55:28.470
I hope we can still smile 
and wave at each other

00:55:28.470 --> 00:55:33.830
Even if we wander deep into the forest

00:55:33.830 --> 00:55:39.060
The sunlight lets us know 
that the dawn is coming

00:55:39.060 --> 00:55:41.690
Even if we can't see it

00:55:41.690 --> 00:55:46.420
The past, future, and present hold hands

00:55:46.420 --> 00:55:49.610
Shining upon the next night

00:55:49.610 --> 00:55:54.730
I'm right here

00:55:54.730 --> 00:55:59.600
Please come to my side

00:55:59.600 --> 00:56:05.300
The desires I left behind still linger

00:56:05.300 --> 00:56:10.580
Even though I go through life 
putting up a strong front

00:56:10.580 --> 00:56:20.510
When I want to see you, 
when I want to embrace you

00:56:20.510 --> 00:56:26.280
I'll use the memories I recall 
and the time we spent together

00:56:26.280 --> 00:56:34.840
To guide me through the future I can't see

00:56:52.070 --> 00:56:53.910
When I scream in despair

00:56:53.910 --> 00:56:57.120
That I want to disappear or run away

00:56:57.120 --> 00:56:59.560
Even on the worst of days

00:56:59.560 --> 00:57:02.350
When I loathed encounters and miracles

00:57:02.350 --> 00:57:05.230
Since I can't pretend they never happened

00:57:05.230 --> 00:57:08.200
I hope that in the end, I can at least feel

00:57:08.200 --> 00:57:14.350
That I'm still glad to be alive

00:57:18.700 --> 00:57:22.840
We can't go back anymore

00:57:29.340 --> 00:57:34.500
I'm going to go

00:57:34.500 --> 00:57:39.210
See? Just watch me

00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:44.980
I'm going to find something 
more important than you

00:57:44.980 --> 00:57:50.280
Because you're the most 
important person to me

00:57:50.280 --> 00:58:00.230
When I want to see you, 
when I want to embrace you

00:58:00.230 --> 00:58:06.030
I'll use the memories I recall 
and the time we spent together

00:58:06.030 --> 00:58:13.250
As a backrest for my heart to lean on

00:58:13.250 --> 00:58:19.150
I'll sing these precious feelings 
for you over and over

00:58:19.150 --> 00:58:26.380
And I'll make them into
 a theme song just for us

00:58:29.110 --> 00:58:31.670
Sorry, I rushed that.

00:58:32.150 --> 00:58:36.150
I'm lame, I don't play fair, 
and I'm a brat...

00:58:36.710 --> 00:58:39.430
I may end up hurting you again,

00:58:39.430 --> 00:58:41.910
and Uenoyama might yell at me again...

00:58:42.650 --> 00:58:46.910
But ever since I heard Mafuyu's 
song, I wanted to change.

00:58:51.050 --> 00:58:52.220
So let me try that aga—

00:58:52.220 --> 00:58:53.830
Okay, I get it.

00:58:53.830 --> 00:58:54.550
Huh?

00:58:57.220 --> 00:58:58.270
Sure.

00:59:00.470 --> 00:59:01.680
For real?

00:59:02.000 --> 00:59:03.130
For real.

00:59:04.310 --> 00:59:06.840
<i>Mafuyu's song is like magic.</i>

00:59:07.300 --> 00:59:10.390
<i>It makes me want to give love another try.</i>

00:59:11.910 --> 00:59:14.440
Ah, Akihiko...

00:59:15.480 --> 00:59:17.110
Let's go home.

00:59:19.070 --> 00:59:21.450
<i>I fell in love one autumn.</i>

00:59:22.620 --> 00:59:28.080
<i>This is an ordinary love story 
that took place one ordinary spring.</i>
